XBRICKSTOP by Tim Shaw (tim@oasis.icl.stc.co.uk)
X
XThis is a simple block-catching game for Unix System V.3 or later.
XThe object of the game is to catch the falling blocks with a paddle before
Xthey build up to the height of the paddle. The speed of the falling blocks
Xgradually increases during the game.
X
XColour is implemented for those that have it. The main block to portability
Xis the use of the poll() system call, which is used here to allow a sub-second
Xdelay.
X
X--- Added modifications for BSD Unixes ---
XI added #ifdefs for BSD to get bs to run on a Sun 3/60 SunOS 3.5.
XThis mainly consisted of using random() instead of srand48(); using
Xselect to delay instead of poll(); and checking for pending input
Xwith ioctl(FIONREAD) instead of using nodelay(win) which is not
Xsupported in BSD curses. It appears to work OK, but has not been
Xextensively tested.
X
X	Bill Randle (billr@saab.CNA.TEK.COM)	Apr 24, 1990
